      "artifacts": {
        "files_modified": [
          "mcp-server/src/gui/model-registry.ts",
          "mcp-server/tests/gui/model-registry.test.ts"
        ]
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T13:31:05Z",
          "note": "model-registry.ts internally calls readModels() inside writeModels() to build the 'existing models' set for deletion detection. This incurs a second filesystem read on every write. A future optimization could accept an optional `previousModels` parameter to allow callers that already hold the registry in memory to skip the re-read. For the current usage pattern (API handler reads then writes in the same request) this is negligible but worth noting."
        },
        {
          "type": "convention",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T13:31:05Z",
          "note": "The _initializeLocalFromDefault() helper is prefixed with a single underscore to signal 'internal only'. The codebase has no established convention for internal helpers (config.ts uses `isNodeError` unprefixed). Aligning to a consistent convention across modules would help new contributors. Since the function is unexported, the underscore is purely documentary."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T13:31:05Z",
          "note": "loadDefaults() currently returns the full merged array including pre-existing local entries as `models`, but only writes to disk when toAdd.length > 0. If the caller re-renders the registry from the returned models array while the disk write is in flight (async), there's a theoretical TOCTOU window. In practice this is fine since the GUI operates sequentially, but a comment noting the write condition would clarify intent."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "qa",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-07-21T13:31:33Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-07-21T13:34:47Z",
