          "note": "getResolvedAssignments() — gracefully handles both missing assignments.json AND missing/unreadable local.json, returning { default_model_slug: null, persona_models: {} } in both cases. Edge-case verified with QA test."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T13:34:47Z",
          "note": "writeModels() calls readModels() internally during the deletion guard phase (step 4). If local.json does not exist at all, the code catches all errors and treats existingModels as []. However, if local.json exists but has a schema validation error, the error is silently swallowed too (empty catch in writeModels). This means a corrupted local.json would allow a write to proceed as if it were empty, potentially bypassing the deletion guard. Consider narrowing the catch to ENOENT-only errors, similar to how readModels() handles it. Not a blocker for current AC, but a latent risk."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T13:34:47Z",
          "note": "No issues with the vi.mock scoping — the mock redirects WORKSPACE_ROOT to a per-test temp directory and is properly cleaned up in afterEach. No test-isolation leakage observed."
