      "summary": [
        "Code review FAIL — one blocking issue: writeModels() uses a bare `catch {}` (lines 202–207) that swallows ALL errors from readModels() during the deletion guard phase. A corrupted local.json (PARSE_ERROR or VALIDATION_ERROR from readModels) silently falls through to existingModels=[], making deletedModels empty and bypassing the deletion guard entirely. The module's documented guarantee — 'rejects deletion of models whose UUID is referenced in assignments.json' — is violated when local.json is corrupted. Fix: narrow the catch to ENOENT-only by re-throwing ApiError exceptions, analogous to the readModels() pattern at line 113–116. One fix-forward comment applied to loadDefaults() clarifying the dead-code path in its readModels catch block."
      ],
      "artifacts": {
        "files_modified": [
          "mcp-server/src/gui/model-registry.ts"
        ]
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "high",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T13:37:18Z",
          "note": "[BLOCKING] writeModels() deletion guard catch (lines 202–207): the bare `catch {}` swallows ALL errors thrown by readModels() — including ApiError PARSE_ERROR and VALIDATION_ERROR — treating them identically to ENOENT. With existingModels=[], deletedModels is always empty, so the deletion guard never fires. A caller that submits a new model list while local.json is corrupt will silently succeed even when it is deleting models referenced in assignments.json. FIX: replace the bare catch with a targeted re-throw for ApiError, keeping only the ENOENT-equivalent silent path. Pattern to follow (same file, readModels line 113): `if (isNodeError(err) && err.code === 'ENOENT') { ... } else { throw err; }`. For readModels(), the ENOENT case comes back as the ApiError wrapping is done after the catch — in writeModels(), readModels() is called directly, so throw any ApiError through: `try { existingModels = await readModels(); } catch (err) { if (!(err instanceof ApiError && err.code === 'READ_ERROR') && !(isNodeError(err) && err.code === 'ENOENT')) throw err; }`"
        },
        {
          "type": "reviewer-applied-fix",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-21T13:37:18Z",
